 that  labour would put forward as an  alternative option well the principles  are as i say out there and very clear  home first  is the first principle that we would  have in our plan  preventative is the second principle in  the plan so that we prevent the problems  um as they arise and prevent them  getting worse and then thirdly on the  workforce and how we improve the terms  and conditions of care workers in  particular quite a lot of that we set  out over the summer when we're dealing  with workplace rights  and just moving on to covid now as we  head into the winter i mean do you agree  with the government getting rid of some  of some of the covert restrictions like  the fact that they've signaled they're  very keen to get rid of pcr tests for  double vax travelers as soon as possible  do you think that should be going as we  head into winter i think everybody wants  to see restrictions  lifted  as best we can  but we've got to be cautious because for  everybody who says to me i want the  restrictions lifted they also say  understandably but i don't want to go  back into another lockdown nobody wants  that so what we've said is follow the  science  be careful be cautious and make sure  that whatever we do we don't go back  into another lockdown  do you agree on that point about pcr  tests i mean the government have said  that they are an unfair cost on families  who want to go away would you like to  see them scrapped as well i think some  of the costs been far too high for the  pcr test but i don't want to get rid of  the idea that tests should be available  to people who need them now travelling  is one aspect of this but what is  vitally important i think is that we  have free tests in our communities so  that people can get tested they know  when they have to isolate and we can get  the virus under control because the most  important thing is that now we have  opened up to a degree that we don't go  back into lockdown would you uh agree  with that do you agree with the  government's plans as well to not push  forward with covert vaccine passports in  england do you think that's the right  decision well the government's plans  change all of the time over the last six  months we've had any number of plans on  vaccine passports last few days we've  seen the government's position change  i think that vaccine passports  should never prevent people getting  essential services health dentistry the  sort of everyday essentials that people  need so shouldn't be a  shouldn't stop people getting those  essentials  possibly for some events they could be  used in conjunction with tests but never  on their own so it should always be an  alternative either a double vaccination  or a negative  test but as i say the most important  thing is that we shouldn't see vaccine  passports stopping people get what is  essential
 

